{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Fix landed on main as 08918c7314 (Gerrit change 1608, LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1).\n\nRoot cause confirmed as triaged: `evals/eval.py::_live_solver` builds ONE PydanticAIRunner before any case fixture exists, so its `LLMConfig.repo_path` is the eval checkout; `runner._effective_config` substitutes only per-request model/limit tuning and preserves that base path, so an injected live runner's agentic filesystem + ticket tools searched the checkout instead of each disposable case repo.\n\nFix: `evals/eval_solver.py::_rerooted` rebuilds the injected PydanticAIRunner rooted at each disposable case store (preserving the offline model_override harness) and clears `tickets_path` so ticket tools read the fixture's own seeded store. Applied inside the `case_store` arm, so it covers completion-verifier, ticket-quality and spec-alignment. Scoped to the eval path — production gate config resolution is untouched, and FakeRunner (which reads no filesystem) passes through unchanged.\n\nTests: new parametrized contract in tests/unit/test_eval_solver.py builds the agent's OWN filesystem tools from the runner config handed to each op and asserts read_file('src/cli.py') returns the fixture content, not the checkout's; verified RED (3 failures: 'runner must be rooted at the case fixture') with the re-root line removed. Gates green: make lint, make typecheck, pytest tests/unit -k eval (202 passed), pytest tests/interfaces -k 'eval or mcp' (315 passed)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786503038283686001,"uuid":"cec9b8f4-443a-4d82-bc9e-4bf5ecc24d70"}